PicWorks is a scientific raster imaging tool designed to allow quick
visualization of raster images.  It has been specifically designed
for use with image cubes with Vicar headers, but has facilities to
handle most non-compressed raster files.

Current Version		#5.013a: Thu Nov  4 15:07:20 MST 1999

The latest distribution of PW is always available for anonymous ftp 
from ftp://east.la.asu.edu/pub/software


INSTALLATION
------------
See the makefile for compile time options and configuration info.
If you have the XPM library and your X include files and libraries
are in the usual places, you should be able to simply type:

% make install

If you don't have XPM or your includes/libraries are in strange 
places, look at the Makefile and follow the directions there.

If all else fails, you should be able to manually compile pw with:

% cc -Ilib lib/*.c pw/*.c -o pw -lX11 -lm

Unless your X include files or libraries are in strange places, in
which case you will need to add -I and -L options to point to these
places.  On a Sun running OpenWindows this means:

% cc -Ilib -I/usr/openwin/include -L/usr/openwin/lib lib/*.c pw/*.c \
  -o pw -lX11 -lm

Or, on under HP-UX, where they do things just a little differently than
the rest of the world, maybe something like this:

% cc -Ilib -I/usr/include/X11R4 -L/usr/lib/X11R4 lib/*.c pw/*.c \
  -o pw -lX11 -lm

The sp directory contains source for the 'sp' SPECPR file requestor,
that lets you browse SPECPR files.  The plot tool in pw uses this
external program to let the user select wavelength and library
spectra from SPECPR.  If you do not wish to use the external program,
there is a limited internal version that can be compiled in by
defining the flag -DINTERNAL_SP at compile time.  The internal
version is no longer supported but will continue to function
indefinitly.  Any enhancements will only go into the external
version.

To date, there is no manual page, but Wendy Calvin and Roger Clark have
put together a tutorial package, available for anonymous ftp from 
speclab.cr.usgs.gov:pub/pw/pw.manual.tar

Send approprate suggestions, requests, bug-reports, monetary disbursements, etc,
to ngorelic@speclab.cr.usgs.gov. 
